    <item>
      <title>Permanent Diverse Skin Tones</title>
      <author>CinnamonClover</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/724239</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/724239#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">839345636eb271d61b6bfee7ad965a4998cabda0</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 23:15:19 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac2ef559159d.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac2d55d4c9e2.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac2d55d16b2d.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac2d55d5b8b0.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac2d55d96d78.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac2d55d309e3.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; EU Support Added&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added EUR-compatible files for European installations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;NOTICE: This patch utilizes AI-assisted coding. ChatGPT was used to decode the original source files, troubleshoot errors, and generate the specific replacement code lines used in this update.&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Permanent Diverse Skin Tones&lt;/h1&gt;This is an alternative version of my Inclusive Skin Tone Mod.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This mod modifies the in-game tanning system to allow for more realistic skin colors while also locking each player's tan level to a permanent value.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The main reason this version exists is to allow multiple players to have different skin tones within the same game. My Inclusive Skin Tone Mod instead locks every player to one general skin tone while keeping a narrower, more realistic range of tanning options.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This version is specifically intended for people who:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Do not want the tanning mechanic at all&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Play multiplayer and would still like to have a diverse range of skin tones&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Share a save file with multiple player characters and want each character to be able to have a different skin color&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;For example, one player with their tan value set to 0 can remain pale-skinned, while another player with their tan value set to 15 can remain dark-skinned.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Because the tanning mechanic is disabled, these skin tones will not fade over time or become darker from sun exposure.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;FEATURES&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Replaces the normal tanning progression with permanent skin tones&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Allows different player characters to use different skin tones in the same town&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Supports tan values from 0 through 15&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Includes multiple skin-tone palettes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Supports both USA and European Welcome Amiibo releases&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Works with both Azahar and Luma3DS / modded 3DS systems&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Compatible with custom texture packs, with some limitations explained below&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;IMPORTANT: REGION-SPECIFIC DOWNLOADS&lt;/h2&gt;This mod now supports both the USA and European versions of Animal Crossing: New Leaf – Welcome Amiibo.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The USA and EUR versions use different executable code, so they require different code.bin files.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You MUST download the version that matches your copy of the game.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;USA game → Download the USA version&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;European game → Download the EUR version&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;Do not use the USA code.bin with a European copy of the game, and do not use the EUR code.bin with a USA copy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Using the wrong regional version may cause the mod to not work correctly or for your game to not boot at all.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;INCLUDED PALETTES&lt;/h2&gt;The download includes multiple different color palettes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each palette is its own version of the mod.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Only use &lt;strong&gt;ONE&lt;/strong&gt; palette / code.bin at a time.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Do not combine multiple included code.bin files together. Choose the palette you want and install only that version.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Included palettes:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Warm Honey&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Cool Rose&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Neutral&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Teak&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Soft Fantasy&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;If you want the skin colors that most closely resemble the original game, use the included Default version.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;SKIN TONE VALUES&lt;/h2&gt;Animal Crossing: New Leaf internally stores the tanning level as a value from 0 to 15.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;However, the game displays those values as 8 visible skin-tone levels.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;0-1 = Tone 1&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;2-3 = Tone 2&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;4-5 = Tone 3&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;6-7 = Tone 4&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;8-9 = Tone 5&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;10-11 = Tone 6&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;12-13 = Tone 7&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;14-15 = Tone 8&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;For example, values 0 and 1 use the same visible skin tone, while values 14 and 15 use the darkest tone in the selected palette.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The contact-sheet images on this page use these same value ranges so you can easily see what each tone will look like before changing your character.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;SETTING YOUR SKIN TONE&lt;/h2&gt;Because this mod disables the normal in-game tanning mechanic, your tan value will no longer change naturally.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Sun exposure will not make your character darker, and your tan will not fade over time.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You must manually set your desired tan value using either:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;ACNL Save Editor&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Vapecord&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;Once set, the mod will keep that value permanent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ACNL Save Editor&lt;/h3&gt;Make a backup of your save before editing it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Open your garden.dat or garden_plus.dat file in ACNL Save Editor.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Select the player you want to modify.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Find the player's Tan value.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set it to a value between 0 and 15.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Save your changes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Restore/import the edited save back into the game.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You can repeat this for each player character in your town and give each one a different skin tone.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For example:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Player 1: 0&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Player 2: 6&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Player 3: 10&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Player 4: 15&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;Each character will keep their selected skin tone permanently.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;VAPECORD&lt;/h3&gt;You can also use Vapecord to change your player's tan value directly in-game.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Use:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Player Codes &amp;gt;Player Save Codes&amp;gt; Player Appearance &amp;gt; Tan&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set the desired value, then save the game normally.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;After the value has been saved, this mod prevents the normal tanning system from changing it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;INSTALLATION&lt;/h2&gt;Before installing, make sure you downloaded the version matching your game region.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;USA copy → USA download&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;European copy → EUR download&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Azahar&lt;/h3&gt;Right-click Animal Crossing: New Leaf – Welcome Amiibo.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Click &lt;strong&gt;Open &amp;gt; Mods Location&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Choose the palette/version you want to use.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Drop that version's entire exefs folder into the mods folder.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Make sure you are only using one version of this mod at a time.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Boot up the game and enjoy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Luma3DS / Modded 3DS&lt;/h3&gt;Make sure Game Patching is enabled in Luma3DS.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Choose the palette/version you want to use.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Take the code.bin file from that version's exefs folder.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Place it on your SD card at the path matching your game region.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;USA:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;code dir="ltr"&gt;luma/titles/0004000000198E00/code.bin&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;EUR:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;code dir="ltr"&gt;luma/titles/0004000000198F00/code.bin&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Make sure there is only one code.bin being used for that title.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Boot up Animal Crossing: New Leaf – Welcome Amiibo and enjoy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;COMPATIBILITY / LIMITATIONS&lt;/h2&gt;This mod currently supports the latest version of:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Animal Crossing: New Leaf – Welcome Amiibo (USA)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Animal Crossing: New Leaf – Welcome Amiibo (EUR)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;Make sure you are using the download that matches your game region.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Other regions or older versions should be considered incompatible unless specifically ported.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This mod is not compatible with other mods that modify the game's executable code, including but not limited to:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;ROM hacks that modify executable code&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Other code.bin mods&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;My Inclusive Skin Tones Mod&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Any other mod that replaces the same executable file&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;Because this mod works by modifying code.bin, installing another code.bin mod will usually overwrite this one or conflict with it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;TEXTURE PACKS&lt;/h2&gt;This mod will work with custom texture packs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;However, some textures in New Leaf are designed around the game's original skin colors. If a texture has been manually color-matched to the default skin tones, it may not perfectly match some of the custom palettes in this mod.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is especially noticeable with things such as:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Certain clothing textures&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Skin-colored accessories&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Textures containing pre-rendered skin colors&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;The default-style palette should remain the closest match to the original game's artwork.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;MULTIPLAYER / MULTIPLE PLAYER CHARACTERS&lt;/h2&gt;One of the main purposes of this version of the mod is allowing different players to retain different permanent skin tones.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For example:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Friend A can use Tan 0-1 and remain pale-skinned&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Friend B can use Tan 14-15 and remain dark-skinned&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;The same applies to multiple player characters living in a single town.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each player character can have their own saved tan value, allowing multiple skin tones to coexist in the same save file.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;ADDITIONAL COLOR PALETTES&lt;/h2&gt;If there is interest, I can add additional palette options in the future, especially fantasy or stylized palettes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you have a specific palette in mind, feel free to leave it in the comments.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A palette can consist of any 8 RGB colors.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For example:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;RGB(255, 220, 200)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;RGB(230, 190, 160)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;RGB(200, 150, 110)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;The eight colors correspond to the eight visible tan levels shown above.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;IMPORTANT NOTES&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Back up your save before using save editors or modifying game files.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Only install one version of this mod at a time.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Do not combine multiple included code.bin files.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The normal tanning mechanic is intentionally disabled.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Changing your skin tone requires ACNL Save Editor or Vapecord.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Make sure you download the version matching your game region.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;USA and EUR versions use different code.bin files.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Texture packs are supported, but some pre-colored textures may not perfectly match custom skin palettes.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;FEEDBACK / REQUESTS&lt;/h2&gt;If you encounter a compatibility issue, visual problem, or have a suggestion for another skin-tone palette, feel free to leave a comment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When reporting an issue, please include:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Whether you are using Azahar or a modded 3DS&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Which palette you installed&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Your game region/version&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Whether you are using any other code.bin or ROM hack mods&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/permanent_diverse_skin_tones.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/permanent_diverse_skin_tones_eur.zip" type="application/zip"/>
